    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46953" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠμᾰθόεις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εσσα</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εν</span> (or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-όεις,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εν</span></span> if <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πύλος</span> (q.v.) be fem.), 
			Ep.
		 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμ-, </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄμαθος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sandy</i>, epith. of the Elean Pylos, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πύλον ἠμαθόεντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					1.93
				</span></i>
			,al., <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				360
			</span></i>: generally 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠμαθόεσσα ἠϊών</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.932
				</span></i>
			. (Deriv. from the name of a river by <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				8.3.14
			</span></i>.)</div>
